notes.body:
The name `loop_init` isn't very descriptive. I suggest a name such as `have_fragments` which starts as `false` and is set to `true` once the first fragment is found.

This clarification would also allow you to reduce a level of indentation after this code by simply returning if there are no fragments (which is presently indicated by `loop_init` still being true).

The duplicated assignments in this block are redundant and can lead to maintenance headaches. The impact of this is lessened if we skip assigning and discarding the `follow_record` memory noted above, but still not great.

Putting it all together, here's my suggestion:

```suggestion:-30+0
    bool have_fragments = false;

    for (; fragment_entry != NULL; fragment_entry = g_list_next(fragment_entry))
    {
        fragment = (follow_record_t*)fragment_entry->data;
        /* First fragment in list, or packet is out of order */
        if(!have_fragments || LT_SEQ(fragment->seq, lowest_seq)) {
            lowest_seq = fragment->seq;
            fragment_mem = fragment;
            fragment_entry_mem = fragment_entry;

            have_fragments = true;
        }
    }

    if(!have_fragments) {
        return false;
    }
```

... and de-indent everything which follows up to my next comment on line 1720.

